      "expected": "The SCL pull-up should be 10 kΩ, consistent with R23 and the listed MPN, rather than 10 Ω.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R28 | 10 | ... MPN= 0603WAF1002T5E"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "SCL0_GPIO45 : ... R28.2(2,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "SDA0_GPIO44 : ... R23.2(2,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R28 +3V3 SCL0_GPIO45 10"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled according to the schematic value, a device pulling SCL low would face an excessively low resistance to 3.3 V, potentially causing excessive sink current and impairing or damaging the I²C interface. The MPN suggests this may be a value-field error rather than the intended fitted value.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U1", "U2", "U15", "U18", "U19", "U22", "U27", "U29", "U30", "U34", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.1", "U15.2", "U15.4", "U22.1", "U22.4", "U35.1", "U35.4", "U36.1"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK1", "ESTOP_SINK2", "ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL", "ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT", "/{slash}LED_EN"],
      "observed": "These parts are represented as SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffers, but their listed MPN is U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R, a different buffer type with a push-pull output rather than an open-drain output.",
      "expected": "The e-stop sink stages require the specified SN74LVC1G07 open-drain behavior; the sourced part should match that output type.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U15 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... acorn-motherboard:SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_SINK1 ... U22.1(/OE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_SINK_ALL ... U35.4(Y,output) U36.1(/OE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is what is fitted, the push-pull outputs do not provide the specified open-drain sink behavior and may actively drive shared sink lines high, compromising the e-stop circuit.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN transceivers’ isolation grounds are explicitly tied together, contradicting the specified isolated CAN interfaces. There is also a 10 Ω versus 10 kΩ discrepancy on the SCL pull-up, and the buffer MPNs do not match the specified open-drain parts."
}

